;;; subject: opendev-terminal-agent-2603 2.3.7 Context Retrieval and Assembly Pipeline: how the code the agent needs is found by tools of rising cost and put together with instructions and history within the token budget
;;; made-from: doc_Base012/docs/Papers-AgentHarness/opendev-terminal-agent/03_context-engineering/03_context-engineering.lisp / p-retrieval-pipeline-need p-retrieval-tool-choice p-explorer-subagent-search p-context-assembly p-final-optimization p-escalation-flow p-bridge-to-tools
;;; members: need tool-choice explorer assembly optimization escalation
;;; elsewhere: none
;;; left-out: the caption of Figure 15
(defrule retrieval -> retrieval-need retrieval-tool-choice retrieval-explorer retrieval-assembly retrieval-optimization retrieval-escalation)
(defrule retrieval-need -> :antithesis retrieval-need/static :nucleus retrieval-need/pipeline)
(defrule retrieval-need/static -> :instruction "従来の一回きりの検索がコードに合わない理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "This works reasonably well for factual question answering over homogeneous corpora, but codebases are fundamentally different.")
(defrule retrieval-need/pipeline -> :instruction "段階的に探索を強める流れを採ることを 1 文で書く" :sample "OpenDev instantiates this principle for software engineering through a four-layer pipeline (Figure 15) that progressively escalates from simple lookups to multi-step agentic search to full context assembly and optimization.")
(defrule retrieval-tool-choice -> :antithesis retrieval-tool-choice/naive :nucleus retrieval-tool-choice/anchor :elaboration-set-member retrieval-tool-choice/mapping)
(defrule retrieval-tool-choice/naive -> :instruction "道具を選ばずに 1 種類で探す失敗を 1 文で書く" :sample "A naive agent defaults to text search for every lookup, a failure mode analogous to the “retrieve-everything” antipattern in traditional RAG [6].")
(defrule retrieval-tool-choice/anchor -> :instruction "問いの中の最も強い手掛かりから道具を選ぶ原則を 1 文で書く" :sample "Effective retrieval instead begins by identifying the strongest anchor in the query: the most specific, highest-signal element that constrains the search space.")
(defrule retrieval-tool-choice/mapping -> :instruction "手掛かりの種類と道具の対応を 1 文で書く" :sample "Symbol names (e.g., AuthController.validate) route to find_symbol, which resolves the definition semantically via LSP; string literals and error messages route to text_search, which performs exact pattern matching; structural patterns (e.g., “all Python if-statements that check is_admin ”) route to ast_search, which matches language-aware templates; and file-path conventions route to list_files for glob-based discovery.")
(defrule retrieval-explorer -> :nucleus retrieval-explorer/delegate :evaluation-s retrieval-explorer/isolation)
(defrule retrieval-explorer/delegate -> :instruction "広い探索を別のエージェントに任せる条件を 1 文で書く" :sample "When the main agent needs broad codebase understanding rather than a pinpoint lookup, it delegates to the Code Explorer subagent (Sections 2.2.7 and 2.4.8), which runs in an isolated context window with access to the same five retrieval tools in read-only mode.")
(defrule retrieval-explorer/isolation -> :instruction "文脈を分ける重要さを 1 文で書く" :sample "Context isolation is critical: intermediate search results (potentially thousands of lines of code) stay in the subagent’s window, and only the distilled summary is returned to the main agent.")
(defrule retrieval-assembly -> :nucleus retrieval-assembly/sources :elaboration-process-step retrieval-assembly/validate)
(defrule retrieval-assembly/sources -> :instruction "探した結果以外に、モデルへ渡す材料を、数と順で 1 文で書く" :sample "Before each model call, ContextPicker assembles the final message list from six ordered sources: (1) the system prompt augmented with selected playbook strategies from the adaptive memory (Section 2.3.6), (2) project-level and user-level persistent rules, (3) inline @file references and image blocks supplied by the user, (4) the conversation history retrieved from SessionManager, (5) system reminders injected at the point of decision (Section 2.3.4), and (6) the current user query.")
(defrule retrieval-assembly/validate -> :instruction "組み上げた構造の検証と修復を 1 文で書く" :sample "The assembled structure is validated by ValidatedMessageList, which enforces structural integrity (every assistant message with tool calls must be followed by matching tool results before the next user turn) and auto-repairs violations with synthetic error placeholders rather than failing outright.")
(defrule retrieval-optimization -> :instruction "組み上げた文脈が、予算に収まるように通る処理を 1 文で書く" :sample "The assembled context passes through ContextCompactor for token-budget enforcement before entering the ReAct reasoning loop.")
(defrule retrieval-escalation -> :instruction "探索の段階が、簡単な問いと複雑な問いで使い分けられることを 1 文で書く" :sample "The four layers form a retrieval pipeline that mirrors the escalation pattern seen in agentic search systems [85]: simple queries resolve at Layer 1 with a single tool call; complex queries escalate to Layer 2’s multi-step search; all results converge at Layer 3’s assembly; and Layer 4 enforces the token budget.")
